        "title": "Long-form · eight voices",
        "kind": {
          "type": "Frame",
          "size": [
            620.0,
            154.0
          ],
          "text": "Every 25 ms segment of both channels has its own voice. Four slow sines (32, 21, 14 and 9 s) set the pulse rate of each segment, four noises their intensity — the periods never line up, so the texture keeps changing for hours. Channel B plays the voices mirrored.\nLimits: A runs 6–26 under a hardware ceiling of 28, so a light touch already starts at 6. B is a narrow 12–20 band with its own Hz range (25–95) and intensity clamp (30–85 %)."
        }
